      "created_at": "2026-05-19T07:03:54Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-05-19T07:03:54Z",
      "body": "With a bit of messing with WASM loading on Durable Object, I got mtcute working in Durable Object. However, the main problem I think is when to trigger the execution of Durable Object. If I'm understanding the pricing of DO correctly, a $5/mo Workers Paid program can only get one DO running 24/7 for a month, and Durable Object is not really designed for that. \n\nThe immediate thought is to use Bot API webhook to trigger execution of DO, however Telegram officially said that multiple session on bot accounts are not supported and will likely make both sessions miss updates. If your bot doesn't need on-demand triggering by commands / message, it's totally feasible to use cron on workers to trigger the bot on a schedule, but otherwise I think it doesn't make sense.",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
